1
00:04:09,090 --> 00:04:15,090
A world beyond your experience, beyond your imagination.

2
00:08:18,181 --> 00:08:24,181
Dune is a action, science fiction, adventure film directed by David Lynch.

3
00:12:27,272 --> 00:12:33,272
In the year 10,191, the most precious substance in
the universe is the spice Melange.

4
00:16:36,363 --> 00:16:42,363
The spice extends life.

5
00:20:45,454 --> 00:20:51,454
The spice expands consciousness.

6
00:24:54,545 --> 00:25:00,545
The spice is vital to space travel.

7
00:29:03,636 --> 00:29:09,636
The spice exists on only one planet in the entire universe, the
vast desert planet Arrakis, also known as Dune.

8
00:33:12,727 --> 00:33:18,727
Its native inhabitants, the Fremen, have long held a prophecy that a man
would come, a messiah who would lead them to true freedom.

9
00:37:21,818 --> 00:37:27,818
Paul Atreides, played by Kyle MacLachlan.

10
00:41:30,909 --> 00:41:36,909
Lady Jessica, played by Francesca Annis.

11
00:45:40,000 --> 00:45:46,000
Gurney Halleck, played by Patrick Stewart.

12
00:49:49,090 --> 00:49:55,090
Shadout Mapes, played by Linda Hunt.

13
00:53:58,181 --> 00:54:04,181
Padisha Emperor Shaddam IV, played by José Ferrer.

14
00:58:07,272 --> 00:58:13,272
Thufir Hawat, played by Freddie Jones.

15
01:02:16,363 --> 01:02:22,363
Dune is a 1984 American epic space opera film written and directed by David
Lynch, and based on the 1965 novel of the same name by Frank Herbert.

16
01:06:25,454 --> 01:06:31,454
It was filmed at the Churubusco Studios in Mexico City.

17
01:10:34,545 --> 01:10:40,545
The soundtrack was composed by the rock band Toto,
with a contribution from Brian Eno.

18
01:14:43,636 --> 01:14:49,636
Its large ensemble cast includes Kyle MacLachlan (in his film debut), Patrick Stewart, Brad Dourif, Dean Stockwell,
Virginia Madsen, José Ferrer, Sean Young, Silvana Mangano, Sting, Linda Hunt, and Max von Sydow.

19
01:18:52,727 --> 01:18:58,727
The setting is the distant future, chronicling the conflict between rival noble families as they
battle for control of the extremely harsh desert planet Arrakis, also known as Dune.

20
01:23:01,818 --> 01:23:07,818
The planet is the only source of the drug melange (spice), which allows prescience and is vital to
space travel, making it the most essential and valuable commodity in the universe.

21
01:27:10,909 --> 01:27:16,909
Paul Atreides is the scion and heir of a powerful noble family, whose appointment to the control
of Arrakis brings them into conflict with its former overlords, House Harkonnen.

22
01:31:20,000 --> 01:31:26,000
Paul is also possibly the Kwisatz Haderach, a messianic
figure expected by the Bene Gesserit sisterhood.

23
01:35:29,090 --> 01:35:35,090
After the novel's initial success, attempts to
adapt Dune as a film began in 1971.

24
01:39:38,181 --> 01:39:44,181
A lengthy process of development followed throughout
the 1970s, during which Arthur P.

25
01:43:47,272 --> 01:43:53,272
Jacobs, Alejandro Jodorowsky, and Ridley Scott unsuccessfully
tried to bring their visions to the screen.

26
01:47:56,363 --> 01:48:02,363
In 1981, executive producer Dino De Laurentiis hired Lynch as director.

27
01:52:05,454 --> 01:52:11,454
The film underperformed at the box office, grossing $30.9
million against a $40–42 million budget.

28
01:56:14,545 --> 01:56:20,545
At least four versions have been released worldwide.

29
02:00:23,636 --> 02:00:29,636
Lynch largely disowned the finished film and had his name removed or
changed to pseudonyms in the credits on certain versions.

30
02:04:32,727 --> 02:04:38,727
Despite receiving mainly negative reviews upon release, the film has developed a cult
following, but opinion varies between fans of the novel and fans of Lynch's films.

31
02:08:41,818 --> 02:08:47,818
The film explores themes of witch, empire, galaxy, rebellion, future.

32
02:12:50,909 --> 02:12:56,909
The tone is thought_provoking and intense.
